  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping DRR support DR Congo 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The coastal area of Muanda is located in the province of Central Kongo in the DR Congo. This area is located between the Congolese marine waters on the Atlantic Ocean and the international port of Matadi upstream from the Congo River estuary. It is bordered to the northwest by the Angolan province of Cabinda, to the northeast by the Cataract District and to the southwest by Angola. The DR Congo has a coastal zone of 40 km. This area, although small, constitutes a mosaic of rich and varied resources and ecosystems with a strategic importance for the economic and social development of the country. The Congolese Atlantic coast has an important mangrove swamp that was established in 1992 as the Mangrove Marine Park.According to a report by the Congolese Ministry of the Environment (2007), the speed of coastal erosion is estimated at 1.5m/year.The DRR-Team has been invited to provide technical assistance on the coastal erosion in Muanda and to provide support in protecting the people who live there.</narrative>
  </description>
